    "cells": {
      "owned_by": "openspec/changes/fire-spread",
      "note": "Design 1-2 and 5: every room's floor in square cells of size_m on the deck's x and z, each with the fuel class of the prop that covers its centre (props, fixtures), else bare. Bare cells take the room's fuel_mj_per_m2 the furnished ones leave, never below bare_min_mj_per_m2. A burning cell rises toward peak x f_O2 with time constant rise_s; an unburnt or knocked-down cell gathers dose (seconds of full exposure) from burning neighbours within two cells (q over the neighbour's peak, times neighbour_weights) and from the hot layer (0 at layer_preheat_k[0] rising to 1 at layer_preheat_k[1]), cooling by dose_cooling_per_s when nothing feeds it, and ignites at its class's dose_s at ignite_kw. A cell below out_below_kw goes out with agent_s of agent on it; with no burning neighbour for smoulder_s after that it is out and cold, and only a burning neighbour or a flashover lights it again (the hot layer preheats only unburnt cells, and only while something in the room burns). aim_height_m is how high over the floor a cone reaches a cell (the flames' base). flame_height_m is the flame drawn at ignition and at peak; smoke_layer_ppm the smoke a hot layer holds, which sets how far it reaches down.",
      "tuned": "Dose figures and the hot layer's preheat range tuned by tools/mockups/fire_cases.mjs on 2026-10-09 so the quarters, door shut, 50 kW seed on a bunk passes 1 MW at 113 s (design 4): every class's dose doubled from the design's first figures, bedding 36 s (not 24) and bare deck 110 s (not 140), and the layer's preheat from 50 C to 180 C (not 100 C to 300 C). See openspec/changes/fire-spread/fire-cases.md.",
